@startuml
title System Shutdown — Arch Flow

actor "Admin\n(SIGTERM/SIGINT)" as Admin
participant "Runner\n(AppRunner)" as Runner
participant "API" as API
participant "Pipeline" as Pipeline
participant "Readers" as Readers
participant "DB" as DB

== Graceful shutdown ==
Admin -> Runner : SIGTERM / SIGINT
Runner -> Runner : set is_shutting_down=True
Runner -> API : handle_exit() + close WS
Runner -> Pipeline : stop() + flush()
Pipeline -> DB : batch INSERT remaining
Runner -> Readers : stop() per-channel
Readers -> Readers : close CAN bus
Runner -> DB : close connection
Runner --> Admin : Shutdown complete

note right of Runner
  VERIFIED AGAINST CURRENT SOURCE CODE
  Graceful sequence complete. Signal handlers registered.
  API drain, pipeline flush, reader stop all correct.
  See SDD_sequence_boot_shutdown & SDD_DETAILED_VERIFICATION.md
end note

@enduml